hing against the weight-loss goal.", "Fat has averaged 91g/day vs the 65g target (140%) across all 74 logged days — it runs about equally high on restaurant and home-cooked days (olive oil, cheese, nuts show up everywhere), so it's a portion-size habit rather than something restaurants specifically drive.", "Only ~15% of daily protein is eaten before noon on average — it's heavily back-loaded into lunch/dinner. Adding 20-30g to breakfast (eggs, yogurt, cheese) would spread muscle-protein-synthesis stimulus more evenly across the day and help with morning satiety.", "Caffeine has been logged at/after the 16:00 cutoff 18 time(s) across the tracked period — your own baseline flags that cutoff as the sleep-friendly line, worth tightening even without a clean sleep-quality signal yet tying the two together.", "Folate averaging 187 vs a ~400 target over the last 6 day(s) (47%) — tracked weekly, not daily (a slow-reserve nutrient) — add leafy greens, legumes on a lighter day to bring the average up.", "Average logged sleep is 7.4h across 76 nights tracked — an established trend at this point, not a sample. 43/76 nights (57%) landed in the 7-9h target band.", "9 ejaculation event(s) logged in the last 14 days — aiming for roughly every 1-2 days (8-14 over a 14-day span) tracks best with the sperm-quality research.", "Weight is -0.45 kg vs. the 2026-06-27 baseline, 3.0 kg from the 76-78 kg target range — pace is steady but slower than the 0.4 kg/week goal; tightening portions on non-restaurant days would help most."]}